# XSH getnetent(), getnetbyname(), getnetbyaddr(), setnetent() and endnetent() (one page)
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The standard guarantees no entry in these databases, so the tests use whatever
# entries exist and are NOTINUSE when there are none.

assertion  XSH.getnetent.001
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Reading entries one at a time after the open call with 0 ends with a null pointer, and opening again with 0 gives the same sequence of entries.
note       NOTINUSE when the database has no entry; the suite assumes nothing about which entries exist.
test       t/001-sequence-rewind.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.002
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Every entry getnetent() returns has non-null n_name and n_aliases, and n_aliases ends with a null pointer.
note       NOTINUSE when the database has no entry; the suite assumes nothing about which entries exist.
test       t/002-entry-shape.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.003
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       getnetbyname(name) with the n_name of the first entry returns that entry (name, address type and number equal).
note       NOTINUSE when the database has no entry; the suite assumes nothing about which entries exist. The first entry is used because it comes first whatever way names are matched.
test       t/003-lookup-name.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.004
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       getnetbyaddr(net, type) with the n_net (host byte order) and n_addrtype of the first entry returns that entry.
note       NOTINUSE when the database has no entry; the suite assumes nothing about which entries exist. The first entry is used because it comes first whatever way keys are matched.
test       t/004-lookup-key.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.005
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       getnetbyname("pc-no-such-network-zz") and getnetbyaddr(1, -1) return a null pointer.
note       These hold whatever the database holds.
test       t/005-not-found.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.006
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       After the open call with a non-zero argument and one read, every descriptor that was not open before has FD_CLOEXEC set.
note       NOTINUSE when the implementation opens no descriptor. Only the descriptors the call opened are examined.
test       t/006-fd-cloexec.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.007
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       After the open call with a non-zero argument and one read, the end call leaves none of the descriptors that call opened open.
note       NOTINUSE when the implementation opens no descriptor.
test       t/007-end-closes.c

assertion  XSH.getnetent.008
anchor     functions/getnetent.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With a non-zero argument to the open call, reading every entry gives the same sequence as with 0.
note       NOTINUSE when the database has no entry; the suite assumes nothing about which entries exist.
test       t/008-stayopen-sequence.c
